        // Actually buggy: pot accumulates without reset, so pot = total tickets * 10 - (wins * 1?) Wait: In buggy, pot is never reset, but pot is still increased by 10 on each play(). On win, contract transfers 1 to bank and (pot - 1) to player. So pot remains unchanged after win? No, pot is not reset, but the transfer subtracts from balance, not pot. So pot just grows by 10 every call, regardless of wins. So pot = numCalls * 10. But balance = initial 0 + numCalls*10 - wins*1 - sum of (pot_before_win - 1) for wins.
